@startuml ssh-agent-topology
' SSH-agent topology after the eng#295 proxy-only cutover (Linux).
' Companion to piggy FDR 0001 (docs/features/0001-proxy-only-agent-universal-front.md),
' eng#295, and posh FDR 0014 (posh docs/features/0014-stable-forwarded-agent-endpoint.md).
'
' Regenerate the rendered image with:  plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/ssh-agent-topology.puml
' The .puml is the source of truth; the .svg beside it is generated.

title SSH-agent topology — post eng#295 proxy-only cutover (Linux)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam nodeBorderColor #666
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #444
  roundCorner 8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #B8A100
}

node "Workstation — the only host with a PIV card" as ws {
  card "YubiKey\nPIV slot 9A / 9D" as yk
  rectangle "**piggy-agent.sock**\n= SSH_AUTH_SOCK\ncard-backed; the sole agent\n(Linux mux retired, piggy#215)" as pa #E9FBE9
  yk -down-> pa : PCSC
}

node "is-ssh-host — no card; agent arrives forwarded" as host {
  rectangle "**proxy-only piggy-agent**\nlistens: ssh_client-agent.sock\n= host SSH_AUTH_SOCK\n(setSshAuthSock, --proxy-only)" as mux #E8F0FF

  rectangle "#3 posh endpoint\n$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/posh/agent/sock\nfixed path; survives posh\nreconnect / roam" as posh #EFEAFB
  rectangle "#2 RemoteForward'd piggy\n~/.local/state/ssh/piggy-agent.sock\n= PIGGY_AUTH_SOCK\nfixed path; per-connection" as fwd #EFEAFB
  rectangle "#1 sshd ForwardAgent\n~/.ssh/agent/s.*.sshd.*\nPATH VARIES; per-connection" as sshd #FFECEC

  mux -down-> posh : upstream\n(degrade)
  mux -down-> fwd  : upstream\n(degrade)
}

' How the workstation agent reaches the host, by access path.
pa -down-> posh : `posh ssh host`\n(posh mux endpoint)
pa -down-> fwd  : `ssh host`\n(eng RemoteForward)
pa .down.> sshd : `ssh host`\n(OpenSSH ForwardAgent)

note right of sshd
  **eng#295 lived here.**
  The fish first-wins rendezvous
  latched onto this socket — path
  varies and it dies with the TCP
  connection. The proxy-only mux
  NEVER lists it, so the latch is
  **structurally impossible**.
end note

note bottom of mux
  Upstreams are **complementary by access path**
  (#3 when reached via posh, #2 on plain `ssh host`)
  and **redundant in keys** (both resolve to the
  workstation's piggy). Degrade serves whichever is
  live; first-wins dedup lists the shared key once.
  This is posh#103's host-global rendezvous.
end note

legend bottom
  == Cutover decisions ==
  **1 — SSH_AUTH_SOCK ownership (eng <-> posh) — RESOLVED 2026-08-23.**
  posh keeps its per-session export UNCONDITIONAL (posh stays
  eng-agnostic); eng's shell-init SSH_AUTH_SOCK (mux) runs AFTER
  the posh session's spawn env and overrides it. So the mux is
  the **sole front** on eng hosts, posh sessions included (they
  gain the degrade-select over posh + fwd); posh's direct export
  is the unmanaged-host fallback. posh FDR 0014 documents it.
  (eng confirms the shell-init override fires per posh-session shell.)

  **2 — `piggy health` targeting — DEFINED.** health prefers
  PIGGY_AUTH_SOCK, so a bare run probes #2 (card-backed),
  not the mux. The mux-targeting invocation
  (env -u PIGGY_AUTH_SOCK SSH_AUTH_SOCK=...ssh_client-agent.sock)
  is documented in eng-ssh(7); FDR 0001 accepted 2026-08-25.
endlegend

@enduml
